Day10🔄 Reverse a Number / Palindrome Number Checker

A beginner-friendly Python program that reverses a number using mathematical operations and checks whether the number is a palindrome.
A palindrome number reads the same from the front and from the back, such as 121, 1221, or 1331.
The program also handles negative numbers using abs() and allows the user to check multiple numbers until they enter q.

📌 Features
🔢 Accepts a number from the user
🔄 Reverses the number using a while loop
🧮 Uses % to extract digits
➗ Uses // to remove digits
🔍 Checks whether the number is a palindrome
➖ Handles negative numbers using abs()
🔄 Allows multiple numbers to be checked
🚪 Allows the user to quit by entering q


